sort:
```
salidas = collect(values(E.utxo))
sort!(salidas, by = o -> (o.dueño, o.valor, ORDEN_ORIGEN[o.origen], o.creada_en_altura, o.creada_en_slot))
for o in salidas:
   "UTXO dueño=$(o.dueño) valor=$(o.valor) origen=$(NOMBRE_ORIGEN[o.origen]) altura=$(o.creada_en_altura == -1 ? "-" : o.creada_en_altura) slot=$(o.creada_en_slot == -1 ? "-" : o.creada_en_slot)"
```

`render_gar(E)`:
```
claves = sort(collect(keys(E.garantias)))
for k in claves:
   g = E.garantias[k]
   pend = sort(g.pendientes, by = p -> (p.importe, p.madura_en_altura, p.madura_en_slot))
   pend_str = join([p.madura_en_altura != -1 ? "$(p.importe)@h$(p.madura_en_altura)" : "$(p.importe)@s$(p.madura_en_slot)" for p in pend], ",")
   ret = sort(g.en_retirada, by = r -> (r.inicio_slot, r.importe))
   ret_str = join(["$(r.importe)@s$(r.inicio_slot)" for r in ret], ",")
   cred = sort(g.creditos, by = p -> (p.importe, p.madura_en_slot))
   cred_str = join(["$(p.importe)@s$(p.madura_en_slot)" for p in cred], ",")
   "GAR clave=$k activo=$(g.activo) pend=[$pend_str] ret=[$ret_str] cred=[$cred_str] congelado=$(g.congelado)"
```

`render_est(E)`:
```
"EST emitido=$(E.emitido) quemado=$(E.quemado) fase=$(NOMBRE_FASE[E.fase]) terminal=$(E.terminal) altura=$(E.altura) slot=$(E.slot) peso_sufijo=$(E.peso_sufijo)"
```

RES computation:
```
function res_por_bloque(bloques, P)
    memo, por_id = construir_validos(bloques, P)
    res = Dict{Int,String}()
    for b in bloques
        if haskey(memo, b.id)
            res[b.id] = "OK"
        else
            p = get(por_id, b.padre, nothing)
            if p === nothing || !haskey(memo, b.padre)
                res[b.id] = "ErrSinPadre"
            else
                r = aplicar(memo[b.padre], b, P)
                res[b.id] = r isa Err ? string(r) : "OK"  # no debería ser OK
            end
        end
    end
    return res
end
```
Wait: if `r isa Err` false (i.e., OK) but b not in memo, that's a contradiction (construir_validos should have added it). Could happen if b.id duplicates another block id in the list: `construir_validos` checks `haskey(memo, b.id) && continue`, so a duplicate id would be skipped and not in memo, but `aplicar` might return OK. Then RES should be "OK" (the duplicate block is valid but already present). Hmm, but duplicate ids in a story? `generar_historia` generates unique ids. Directed cases: X-01's Bgen.id = gid+1 = 2, prefix genesis id 1. Unique. `historia_dos_terminales`: B1 id = pref[3], B2 id = pref[3]+1, post chains start at pref[3]+100 / +200. Unique. So no duplicates. But to be safe, if `aplicar` returns OK for a not-in-memo block due to id collision, I'll record "OK". Fine.

Hmm, actually there's a subtle issue: `construir_validos` returns `memo` keyed by id. If two blocks have the same id, only the first is stored and the second (even if valid) is skipped; `puntas_validas` iterates keys of memo and uses `por_id[id]` which is the LAST block with that id (since `por_id[b.id]=b` overwrites in the loop over all bloques). That could cause inconsistency. But no duplicate ids in our stories.

