Also, the `param` field in CasoLeido is `Dict{String,String}` but `campos` returns `Dict{SubString,SubString}`; assigning to `param` redefines type (function-local). CasoLeido constructor expects `Dict{String,String}`, so passing a SubString Dict will fail conversion? Actually `Dict{SubString,SubString}` is not a `Dict{String,String}`; the struct field is typed `Dict{String,String}`, so construction would error (or convert?). Julia will try `convert(Dict{String,String}, d)`, which errors because no such convert. So I should make `CasoLeido.param::Dict{String,String}` and convert in `campos`, or type the field as `AbstractDict{String,String}` (no). Simplest: make `campos` return `Dict{String,String}` by `String.(...)`:
```
campos(linea) = Dict(String(k) => String(v) for (k,v) in (split(t,"=",limit=2) for t in split(linea)[2:end]))
```
That yields Dict{String,String}. Good. Then `parsear_bloque(c::Dict{String,String},...)` works. Let me redefine `campos` to produce String keys/values.

